1
00:00:00,848 --> 00:00:05,040
>> [clears throat] >> Comrades, you've heard already about the strange

2
00:00:05,040 --> 00:00:07,600
dream that I had last night.

3
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:10,199
But I will come to the dream later.

4
00:00:10,199 --> 00:00:13,639
I have something else to say first.

5
00:00:13,639 --> 00:00:18,199
I do not think, comrades, that I shall be with you for many months longer. And

6
00:00:18,199 --> 00:00:22,480
before I die, I feel it my duty to pass on to you such

7
00:00:22,480 --> 00:00:25,319
wisdom as I have acquired.

8
00:00:25,319 --> 00:00:27,319
I've had a long life.

9
00:00:27,319 --> 00:00:31,720
I've had much time for thought as I lay alone in my stall,

10
00:00:31,720 --> 00:00:36,600
and I think I may say that I understand the nature of life on this earth as well

11
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:39,480
as any animal now living.

12
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:44,639
It is about this that I wish to speak to you. Now, comrades, what is the nature

13
00:00:44,639 --> 00:00:46,600
of this life of ours?

14
00:00:46,600 --> 00:00:48,120
Let us face it.

15
00:00:48,120 --> 00:00:53,319
Our lives are miserable, laborious, and short. We are born,

16
00:00:53,319 --> 00:00:58,040
we are given just so much food as will keep the breath in our bodies,

17
00:00:58,040 --> 00:01:02,439
and those of us who are capable of it are forced to work to the last atom of

18
00:01:02,439 --> 00:01:03,959
our strength.

19
00:01:03,959 --> 00:01:08,240
And the very instant that our usefulness has come to an end, we are slaughtered

20
00:01:08,240 --> 00:01:10,759
with hideous cruelty.

21
00:01:10,759 --> 00:01:16,120
No animal in England knows the meaning of happiness or leisure after he is a year old.

22
00:01:16,120 --> 00:01:18,680
No animal in England is free.

23
00:01:18,680 --> 00:01:22,399
The life of an animal is misery and slavery.

24
00:01:22,399 --> 00:01:24,399
That is the plain truth.

25
00:01:24,399 --> 00:01:27,879
But is this simply part of the order of nature?

26
00:01:27,879 --> 00:01:33,079
Is it because this land of ours is so poor that it cannot afford a decent life

27
00:01:33,079 --> 00:01:35,480
to those who dwell upon it?

28
00:01:35,480 --> 00:01:39,040
No, comrades, a thousand times no!

29
00:01:39,040 --> 00:01:44,120
The soil of England is fertile, its climate is good, it is capable of

30
00:01:44,120 --> 00:01:50,918
affording food in abundance to an enormously greater number of animals than now inhabit it.

31
00:01:50,918 --> 00:01:57,319
This single farm of ours would support a dozen horses, 20 cows, hundreds of

32
00:01:57,319 --> 00:02:01,879
sheep, and all of them living in a comfort and a dignity that are now

33
00:02:01,879 --> 00:02:04,839
almost beyond our imagining.

34
00:02:04,839 --> 00:02:08,574
Why then do we continue in this miserable condition?

35
00:02:08,574 --> 00:02:10,680
>> [clears throat] >> Because nearly the whole of the produce

36
00:02:10,680 --> 00:02:15,040
of our labor is stolen from us by human beings.

37
00:02:15,040 --> 00:02:19,839
There, comrades, is the answer to all our problems. It is summed up in a

38
00:02:19,839 --> 00:02:26,279
single word, man. [clears throat] Man is the only real enemy we have.

39
00:02:26,279 --> 00:02:33,360
Remove man from the scene and the root cause of hunger and overwork is abolished forever.

40
00:02:33,360 --> 00:02:38,480
Man is the only creature that consumes without producing. He does not give

41
00:02:38,480 --> 00:02:44,240
milk. He does not lay eggs. He is too weak to pull the plow. He cannot run

42
00:02:44,240 --> 00:02:46,639
fast enough to catch rabbits.

43
00:02:46,639 --> 00:02:52,079
Yet he is lord of all the animals. He sets them to work. He gives back to them

44
00:02:52,079 --> 00:02:58,639
the bare minimum that will prevent them from starving and the rest he keeps for himself.

45
00:02:58,639 --> 00:03:04,319
Our labor tills the soil. Our dung fertilizes it and yet there is not one

46
00:03:04,319 --> 00:03:07,524
of us that owns more than his bare skin.

47
00:03:07,524 --> 00:03:10,960
>> [clears throat] >> You cows that I see before me, how many

48
00:03:10,960 --> 00:03:15,679
thousands of gallons of milk have you given during this last year?

49
00:03:15,679 --> 00:03:20,399
And what has happened to that milk which should have been breeding up sturdy calves?

50
00:03:20,399 --> 00:03:24,839
Every drop of it has gone down the throats of our enemies.

51
00:03:24,839 --> 00:03:30,279
And you hens, how many eggs have you laid in this last year? And how many of

52
00:03:30,279 --> 00:03:33,600
those eggs ever hatched into chickens?

53
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:39,360
The rest have all gone to market to bring in money for Jones and his men.

54
00:03:39,360 --> 00:03:44,120
And you, Clover, where are those four foals you bore who should have been in

55
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:47,639
the support and pleasure of your old age?

56
00:03:47,639 --> 00:03:52,721
Each was sold at a year old. You will never see one of them again.

57
00:03:52,721 --> 00:03:55,600
>> [clears throat] >> In return for your four confinements and

58
00:03:55,600 --> 00:04:00,839
all your labor in the fields, what have you ever had except your bare rations

59
00:04:00,839 --> 00:04:08,480
and a stall? And even the miserable lives we lead are not allowed to reach their natural span.

60
00:04:08,480 --> 00:04:12,879
For myself, I do not grumble, for I am one of the lucky ones.

61
00:04:12,879 --> 00:04:17,559
I am 12 years old and have had over 400 children.

62
00:04:17,559 --> 00:04:20,440
Such is the natural life of a pig.

63
00:04:20,440 --> 00:04:24,960
But no animal escapes the cruel knife in the end.

64
00:04:24,960 --> 00:04:29,159
You young porkers who are sitting in front of me, every one of you will

65
00:04:29,159 --> 00:04:33,200
scream your lives out of the block within a year.

66
00:04:33,200 --> 00:04:35,951
To that horror we all must come. Cows,

67
00:04:35,951 --> 00:04:36,519
[clears throat]

68
00:04:36,519 --> 00:04:40,320
pigs, hens, sheep, everyone.

69
00:04:40,320 --> 00:04:44,159
Even the horses and the dogs have no better fate.

70
00:04:44,159 --> 00:04:50,879
You Boxer, the very day that those great muscles of yours lose their power, Jones

71
00:04:50,879 --> 00:04:57,320
will sell you to the who will cut your throat and boil you down for the foxhounds.

72
00:04:57,320 --> 00:05:02,360
As for the dogs, when they grow old and toothless, Jones ties a brick round

73
00:05:02,360 --> 00:05:05,840
their necks and drowns them in the nearest pond.

74
00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:11,120
Is it not crystal clear then, comrades, that all the evils of this life of ours

75
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:14,440
spring from the tyranny of human beings?

76
00:05:14,440 --> 00:05:19,182
Only get rid of man and the produce of our labor would be our own.

77
00:05:19,182 --> 00:05:23,559
>> [clears throat] >> Almost overnight we could become rich and free.

78
00:05:23,559 --> 00:05:25,440
What then must we do?

79
00:05:25,440 --> 00:05:32,080
Why, work night and day, body and soul, for the overthrow of the human race.

80
00:05:32,080 --> 00:05:37,559
That is my message to you, comrades, rebellion.

81
00:05:37,559 --> 00:05:40,142
I do not know when that rebellion will come.

82
00:05:40,142 --> 00:05:43,799
>> [clears throat] >> It might be in a week or in a hundred years.

83
00:05:43,799 --> 00:05:49,559
But I know, as surely as I see this straw beneath my feet, that sooner or

84
00:05:49,559 --> 00:05:53,120
later justice will be done.

85
00:05:53,120 --> 00:05:58,919
Fix your eyes on that, comrades, throughout the short remainder of your lives.

86
00:05:58,919 --> 00:06:04,200
And above all, pass on this message of mine to those who come after you, so

87
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:09,519
that future generations shall carry on the struggle until it is victorious.

88
00:06:09,519 --> 00:06:14,159
And remember, comrades, your resolution must never falter.

89
00:06:14,159 --> 00:06:17,039
No argument must lead you astray.

90
00:06:17,039 --> 00:06:21,879
Never listen when they tell you that man and the animals have a common interest,

91
00:06:21,879 --> 00:06:26,480
that the prosperity of the one is the prosperity of the others.

92
00:06:26,480 --> 00:06:29,000
It is all lies.

93
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:35,080
Man serves the interests of no creature except himself. And among us animals,

94
00:06:35,080 --> 00:06:40,440
let there be perfect unity, perfect comradeship in the struggle.

95
00:06:40,440 --> 00:06:46,200
All men are enemies. All animals are comrades.

96
00:06:46,200 --> 00:06:50,279
>> At this moment, there was a tremendous uproar.

97
00:06:50,279 --> 00:06:56,080
While Major was speaking, four large rats had crept out of their holes and

98
00:06:56,080 --> 00:06:59,799
were sitting on their hindquarters listening to him.

99
00:06:59,799 --> 00:07:04,480
The dogs had suddenly caught sight of them, and it was only by a swift dash

100
00:07:04,480 --> 00:07:08,399
for their holes that the rats saved their lives.

101
00:07:08,399 --> 00:07:11,399
Major raised his trotter for silence.

102
00:07:11,399 --> 00:07:15,919
>> Comrades, here is a point that must be settled.

103
00:07:15,919 --> 00:07:22,759
The wild creatures, such as rats and rabbits, are they our friends or our enemies?

104
00:07:22,759 --> 00:07:24,759
Let us put it to the vote.

105
00:07:24,759 --> 00:07:27,839
I propose this question to the meeting.

106
00:07:27,839 --> 00:07:30,720
Are rats comrades?

107
00:07:30,720 --> 00:07:35,559
>> The vote was taken at once, and it was agreed by an overwhelming majority that

108
00:07:35,559 --> 00:07:38,000
rats were comrades.

109
00:07:38,000 --> 00:07:42,639
There were only four dissentients, the three dogs and the cat, who was

110
00:07:42,639 --> 00:07:46,679
afterwards discovered to have voted on both sides.

111
00:07:46,679 --> 00:07:49,879
Major continued.

112
00:07:49,879 --> 00:07:50,000
>> I have little more to say.
